Generic single-database configuration.

Alembic is initialized from the first commit (§6.13) — the schema will churn for months,
and retrofitting migrations after it stabilizes is the expensive version of this decision.

To generate a new revision after changing `tracker/db/models.py`:

    make migrate ARGS="revision --autogenerate -m 'describe the change'"

Autogenerate diffs must be hand-reviewed before committing, not shipped unread — check
table/column order for foreign-key safety, check that `downgrade()` drops in the reverse
order, and check that enum/constraint names came out through the naming convention in
`tracker/db/models.py` rather than as dialect-generated names.

Then apply and format:

    make migrate
    make format

`make format` matters here specifically: `op.create_table(...)` calls for wide tables
autogenerate onto single long lines, which fails `make lint`'s `ruff format --check` until
reformatted.
